    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and both tests pass (`pytest -q`: 2 passed).\n\nHow it meets each requirement:\n\n1. **Timeouts:** `httpx.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)` gives connect 5s and read, write and pool 30s. I set it on both the OpenAI client and the HTTP client. The OpenAI SDK attaches its own timeout to every request, so setting it only on the HTTP client would have no effect.\n2. **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n3. **Logging:** a `\"request\"` event hook on the HTTP client logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The SDK sends each retry through that same client, so retries are logged too.\n4. **Transport:** the HTTP client is built with `transport=transport`. Passing `None` falls back to the normal default.\n\nThe HTTP client is the SDK's `DefaultHttpxClient`, so the SDK's defaults for connection limits and redirects still apply. No dependencies were added.\n\nI also added `tests/test_build_client.py`. It uses a stub transport that always returns HTTP 500 and checks that:\n- the call is attempted 3 times (1 + 2 retries) and each attempt is logged once as `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`;\n- the timeouts are set correctly on both clients and on the outgoing request."
